 when we get to season four and aaron  does  the exact same thing that rainer did by  attacking a society for what he believes  to be a purpose of greater good  am i going to blame the new eren that he  creates as a result of that  and my answer is absolutely not gabi is  simply doing what she thought was  justified and thinking exclusively from  her perspective that is  very hard to argue with especially  because aaron at this stage is 100  an antagonist like we all get that right  the moment he decided to kill innocent  civilians for  whatever purpose this turns out to be he  was lost i don't think there's any  redemption for him and just as he said  to rainer they  are now the same which in a really  intriguingly twisted way now sort of  makes guard be our protagonist because  she is the latest victim in this vicious  cycle a cycle where she was radicalized  by the actions of eren who was  radicalized by the actions of rainer who  was radicalized by his society which was  radicalized by the actions of ancient  elder it's a cycle that spans  i think thousands of years and gabi is  just our latest descendant of that  so my question becomes now that aaron is  irredeemable will it actually be up to  gabi to be the one to break this cycle  right now looks like gabi is on the  exact same path as aaron and will  continue to commit atrocity after  atrocity until someone is eventually  radicalized by her and seek revenge in  this new catastrophic threat but given  the meta information that this is the  final season i'm inclined to believe  that things will end with gabi and her  generation and i guess i should say at  this point that no i have not read the  manga so i could be very very wrong  about this and just have very minimal  desire to read the manga because i enjoy  the attack on titan anime experience so  all of the margaritas can now proceed to  go  well he's or wrong in the comments below  but this is just how i feel at this  particular point which to reiterate 